 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The drowning (73:9-12) is not glossed. Al-Muyassar's first-person wording for 73 and As-Sa'di's mention of Nuh calling them by night and by day are not used. STAGING v4: Nuh is a blue drop labelled Nuh, never a figure; no plate starts on his name and no close-up or pan is made on his drop (wide holds only while he is named or speaks). His people are three faceless men in dark robes in a plain town by day (the sources name no place). c1 (71-72): 71:1-5 is addressed to the Prophet ﷺ (recite to them): camera only. Nuh speaks to his people (71:6, then at each new sentence 71:17, 71:20, 71:23, 71:30, 72:4, 72:12; his speech arcs point at them); his people make no gesture inside his words; his challenge (71:20-33) and the conditional 72:1-2 are not acted. An hourglass for do not give me respite (71:32-33) and a seal plate for my reward is only from Allah (72:8-11). c2 (73), the ark: they shake their heads (73:1, they denied him), turn on 73:2 and leave on 73:3, so nobody is on the stage at the flood; the ark comes in on 73:4 in the centre, never on the spot the deniers left (so they never read as those with him), and Nuh moves to it (73:5, saved in the ark; those with him are inside and not drawn, so they are not counted); on 73:9 the sky darkens (As-Sa'di: the sky poured water) and the flood rises over the empty town, the ark floating with Nuh's drop above the water. Nobody is drowned or hurt; the camera stays wide; an hourglass for see how was the end (73:16-17, addressed to the Prophet ﷺ). c3 (74), split from c2 at the verse boundary with a new title: a later nation (three faceless men in dark robes) in a town; the messengers after Nuh are not drawn (several prophets of different eras); the camera is wide on 74:5 (messengers) and on 74:8-9 (they came to them with clear proofs), with no pan toward an empty side, so no figure reads as a messenger; no gesture inside the negated 74:10-12; they shake their heads on 74:14 (what they had denied before); a seal plate for We seal the hearts (74:19-22) and they turn away on 74:22 (the transgressors)."
 },
